{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/93592-vs-the-dark-kingdom-of-jade","id":93592,"title":"Vs the Dark Kingdom of Jade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T11:10:25-07:00","id":93592,"title":"Vs the Dark Kingdom of Jade","content":"Okay I leeeerved the whole idea that the First Emperor of China's extravagant Death preparations results in him having the Forces he Needs to realistically have a potential shot at conquering the Underworld, in time. Its really badass that he has an army of glowing brilliant colored Immortals made of stone, and that he is opressing the dickens out of his corner of the Underworld. I always felt it would be a great idea to have say a Werewolf/ Hengeyokai game about the player's pack realizing &quot;gee wiz if any of our relatives become a ghost they are oppressed/enslaved/turned into Building Material so why not do something about it using our pack.&quot; I think it would be really cool for Shapeshifters to actually go against the government of the Underworld, with their attitude that dead or alive these are just mortals there is a lot of cool room for interesting storytelling. This is one of the rare chances to actually fight an actual empire, any sort of equivalent battle in the Living World results in shadowy campaigns that the world never hears about, but in the Underworld they could really change an entire region. The Jade Kingdom has really no threat that can compare to their Immortal Guard, anything that can realistically fight won't because they only exist in the Labyrinth but Werewolves are a trump card that could turn the tide of any battle down there.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have to even be about a Werewolf/Fera game, I could see it working with many of the others like Mage, Hsien, Kueijin or Mummy. I just think it would be really cool to do a full on Chronicle were the Dark Kingdom of Jade is the main antagonist. To me wraith would fit really well in pretty much all the other gamelines. A game a Player group of Vampires for instance would take less tampering to do a crossover with Wraith then say Mage.<br /> <br /> I wish their was more on the Dark Kingdom of Jade in Revised, the setting was introduced really early on, 1995, so they didn't really have much on how the CWOD worked. But after the book we finally got more and more on the various settings in Asia. For instance it would be nice to see a discussion on how Yu-Huang technically would hold the title of Yama King as he owns his own realm in the Underworld (His Palace, TiYu itself, and the Shadowlands territories), and is a Malfean (Seeing as Malfeans are among the beings that take the Title of Yama King). I think it would be cool if they mention things like spirits in the Dark Kingdom of Jade, for instance I would have Mukade on the loose after the 6th Maelstrom broke out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}